# Symbolic Links to Executables from /usr/local/bin

Symbolic links to Samba tools from /usr/local/bin.
They are dedicated to locally built samba-3.6.25
with prefix /usr/local/samba.

```bash
sudo ln -s ../samba/bin/pdbedit pdbedit3
sudo ln -s ../samba/bin/smbpasswd smbpasswd3
sudo ln -s ../samba/bin/testparm testparm3
```

Here, brief of notes for pdbedit3, smbpasswd3,
and testparm3.

## pdbedit3

The Samba password manipulating tool in detail.
Samba passwords are stored into
/usr/local/samba/private/passdb.tdb.

## smbpasswd3

The Samba password manipulating tool.
Add user, and modify password in
/usr/local/samba/private/passdb.tdb.

## testparm3

Test Samba configuration in /usr/local/samba/lib/smb.conf.

## How About Other Tools

If you want to use other tools, execute tools with full
path. For example,

```bash
/usr/local/samba/bin/tdbdump /usr/local/samba/private/secrets.tdb
```

Or, create symbolic link for convenience.
